==French==

===Etymology===
Originally {{term|l'||an apocopic form of ''la'', ''la'' before a vowel|lang=fr}} and {{term|endemain|lang=fr}}, from {{term|en|lang=fr}} and {{term|demain|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-lendemain.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|/lɑ̃dmɛ̃/|lang=fr}}, {{X-SAMPA|/lA~d.mE~/}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# the [[day]] [[after]], the [[next]] [[day]], the [[morrow]].{{jump|day after|a}}
#: ''J'ai un examen le '''lendemain''' de mon mariage''
#:: ''I have an exam the '''day after''' my wedding''

